:name: vaios on-target unit tests (Renode STM32F4)
:description: Run the PIL UNIT_TESTS runner against the real kernel on a
:            generic STM32F4 model and stream the UART results to the log.
:
: Build first:
:   cmake -S . -B build_pil -DNAVHAL=ON -DEXAMPLES=ON -DVAIOS_EXAMPLE=UNIT_TESTS
:   cmake --build build_pil
: Then, from the repo root:
:   renode --console --disable-xwt -e "include @tools/renode_unit_tests.resc"
: Override the ELF with:  -e "$bin=@<path-to>/main"  before the include.

using sysbus
$bin?=@build_pil/examples/main

mach create "vaios_pil"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32f4.repl
cpu PerformanceInMips 84

# Stream USART2 TX (the test runner's polling-UART output) into the Renode log.
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2 Antmicro.Renode.Analyzers.LoggingUartAnalyzer

sysbus LoadELF $bin
emulation RunFor "4.0"
quit
